1.3.1-snapshot
  Emission override for maneuvers and danger reactions
    Emission override keeps AlifeTactics from pulling stalkers out of shelter in an emission or a psi storm, with a switch on Maneuvers and on Danger.

  Combat
    Maneuvers
      - Added Emission override. During an emission or a psi storm no maneuver starts and the one in progress ends. A separate toggle, default on.
  Perception
    Sound
      - Fixed Movement noise and Handling noise alerting a stalker who is set to leave you alone, as in a peace zone or after a bribe.
    Danger
      - Added Emission override. During an emission or a psi storm a calm stalker stays put after a noise, a hit or a nearby bullet, and Distant hits is off. A separate toggle, default on.
      - Fixed calm stalkers leaving their post with their weapon drawn at every mutant attack or enemy bullet heard within 30 m. On GAMMA they put it away 7 s later and drew it again at the next sound, over and over. Such a sound now counts only beside a danger they perceive, as in vanilla. Your own noise and gunfire work as before.
      - Fixed a stalker standing frozen for several seconds when a noise reached him in the middle of a corpse check.
  Mechanics
    Ammo
      - Changed AP ammo to follow the modpack's rank table. On GAMMA and EFP only veterans and up fire it, as in vanilla.

  Fixes
    - Removed the Grenade dodge radius row, because vanilla already dodges a grenade across the same radius.

  Update check
    - Added an update check. The mod asks GitHub for a newer release and shows it at the foot of the MCM page and in a daily PDA message.
      Check for update on the Development page asks right away.

1.3.0
  Mutant combat, a shared decision model, and sharper stalker senses
    Mutants now fight with new and revived moves, leaps, a claw, a rear strike, a gravity throw and a cloak, each taken when you give an opening.
    Stalkers and mutants share a decision model. Intelligence rises with rank, and Personality comes from the faction or the species.
    Other things you will notice. Stalkers hear you before they see you, notice a missed knife swing, retreat to real cover, mount looted scopes, and their guns jam only from wear.

  Combat
    General
      - Added Intelligence for stalkers, the chance that a stalker reads a moment of the fight right. It rises with rank.
      - Added Personality for stalkers, the set of actions a stalker carries, rolled from his faction's chances when he comes online.
      - Changed flee to a separate chance, which falls as Intelligence rises. A sharp stalker sometimes flees, and a dull one flees more often.
    Maneuvers
      - Changed the takeover so a stalker who comes online without a job, as at a full Warfare base, gets maneuvers once he enters combat.
      - Changed retreat to give ground to the best cover behind the stalker, and to end when he reaches it.
      - Changed reload cover to duck behind the nearest cover that breaks the watcher's line.
      - Fixed a downed enemy counting as a threat, which made stalkers back away from him and kept the vanilla finisher from reaching him.
    Commitment
      - Changed Liquidate to draw from the shared start budget. A crowd cannot all fire through your reload at once.
      - Added your back turned as an opening for Liquidate and the Push.
    Conduct
      - Changed cover posture to hold each crouch or stand decision longer. Stalkers shuffle their stance less under fire.
      - Changed cover posture and weapon spacing to follow a stalker's discipline. Militarized factions usually have it, and scavengers usually do not.

  Effectiveness
    - Changed each rank curve to a base slider plus a percent per rank slider. Moved sliders on these pages reset to their defaults once.
    Reaction
      - Fixed target lead ignoring the loaded round's bullet speed. Stalkers again lead a moving target by the round's real flight time.

  Perception
    Sound
      - Added hearing before first contact. A stalker now stores your loud sounds before he has seen you, and the engine runs its own cover and search on them.
      - Changed a heard shot to run the engine's full plan of cover, look-out, detour and search. The Enemy gunfire toggle is gone.
      - Changed Neutral gunfire alert to govern a neutral's reaction to your bullet striking near him.
      - Fixed Sound and Attempted murder logging an engine error when vanilla's list of online stalkers kept an id the game had reused for an artefact.
    Danger
      - Added Attempted murder. A missed knife swing alerts the stalker it was meant for, and a hostile who sees you fights. Its own toggle, default on.
      - Fixed a seated stalker who heard a noise walking off facing away. He now faces the noise.
      - Changed Distant hits to answer enemies only. A neutral's stray hit is no longer answered as an attack.
      - Removed the Player ranges toggle. Every shipped config sets the actor danger tables equal to the normal ones.
      - Fixed vanilla bug "hit shooter identity". A stalker hit by a bullet now looks at the shooter and takes cover from him. Listed on the Fixes tab.
      - Fixed vanilla bug "friendly-fire aim at mutants". A stalker checks his line of fire against a chimera's or burer's body, not its feet. Listed on the Fixes tab.
      - Fixed vanilla bug "player bias" out of the box. Player target pull now defaults to the weight of any NPC enemy, and 900 restores the vanilla magnet.

  Mechanics
    Healing
      - Changed Healing to work with GAMMA's Anti Lag, where a stalker healed once and then never used a medkit again.
    Attachments
      - Added attachment mounting. A stalker out of a fight fits the scope, silencer or grenade launcher that suits his pistol or rifle.
      - A mounted scope tightens his aim when he shoots from a stop, by the scope bonus of the base game.
      - Companions mount what they loot, and what you hand a companion stays as you gave it.
    Jamming
      - Changed Jamming to drop only the fake jam the modded exes inject for NPCs. A worn NPC weapon now misfires by its condition, the same way yours does.

  Mutants
    The system runs on a batch of xray-monolith engine changes and stays off on an exe without the monster hooks. More engine work is in progress.
    General
      - Added Intelligence for mutants, the chance that a mutant reads a moment of the fight right. It rises with the map's danger rank.
      - Added Personality for mutants, the set of moves an individual carries, rolled from its species' chances. 2 chimeras of a pack fight differently.
      - Added Wild, a slider for how much a mutant's numbers vary between individuals, up to a different set of numbers for each one.
      - Added pacing. A mutant spaces its moves apart, and once one mutant's leap, strike or throw hits you, the others hold their next move on you for a few seconds.
      - A mutant reads the weapon in your hands and your aim from where you look.
      - Fixed vanilla bug "chimera re-jump". A chimera or lurker now rests after each jump, where vanilla let it jump again the moment it landed. Listed on the Fixes tab.
    New moves
      - Added the leap family, 7 leaps for the chimera, lurker, cat, dog, snork, pseudodogs and bloodsucker. Personality decides which leaps an individual carries.
      - High leap springs up at you when you stand on a rock or a ledge above the mutant.
      - Punishing leap strikes when you aim at the mutant, reload, sprint or turn your back.
      - Hunting leap and Feral leap steer in the air to follow you while you move. Feral leap gives no warning.
      - Catching leap and Cutoff leap jump to where you will be. Cutoff leap gives no warning.
      - Closing leap brings a bloodsucker to you when you stand on a perch or aim at him, then he strikes with his claws.
      - High, Hunting and Catching leap crouch first. A chimera or a lurker has no crouch, and its leaps all come without warning.
      - Added the claw, a point-blank pounce for the chimera and lurker.
      - Added Backstrike, a spin strike when you get behind a chimera, lurker, burer or controller.
      - Added flee. A mutant near death may run from the fight when you are far enough, and a cornered one fights on.
    Managed moves
      - Changed the burer's gravity throw to fire when you look away from him or cannot answer, and to hold while you face him.
      - Changed the bloodsucker's cloak to vanish when you aim at him or hit him.
    Influenced moves
      - Added ability variation. Wild spreads each species' ability numbers: burer gravity and telekinesis, controller psi tube, stamina and auras, poltergeist detection.

  MCM
    - Changed every page description, label and tooltip to plain words that explain each system and name what drives it.
    - Fixed the version and compatibility line showing on the second Combat page. It now closes the first page.

  Development
    - Added the mutant rows to the debug HUD and the world trace.
    - Added a DEBUG trace line for each mutant move the mod influences, triggers or blocks.
    - Added the hit-reply line to the world trace: when a stalker you hit saw you, picked you as his target, and fired back.
    - Added the distance to each danger mark in the danger trace.

1.2.1
  Push and Pull, Faction flavor, and maneuvers in every fight near you
    Behaviors is a new page. The Push presses an enemy who cannot answer, and the Pull takes a weak stalker back to cover. Faction flavor sets how each faction fights.
    Maneuvers now run in any stalker fight near you, under a shared budget. 2 targeting fixes merged into X-Ray turn a hit stalker on his shooter.
    Other things you will notice. Stalkers keep their footing when hit, glance at creatures they hear, react to noise in proportion, and fewer danger bugs freeze or silence them.

  Combat
    - Added Faction flavor. Each faction fights its own way, and whether a stalker routs, falls back, presses or plants is a chance set per faction.
    - Fixed vanilla bug "monolith combat stance". Fighters on the vanilla Monolith combat scheme flip between crouch and idle far less often.
    Maneuvers
      - Changed maneuvers to run in every stalker fight near you, where they used to run only in yours. Each maneuver keys on the enemy who makes it real, and fights with mutants stay vanilla.
      - Added one shared budget for everything the mod starts near you, split between actions against you and actions against NPCs. A mass battle cannot flood either side.
      - Added Hit reaction hold. A standing stalker hit mid reaction keeps his feet planted until the hit animation ends, where he used to slide across the ground.
      - Changed Reload Cover to answer any watching enemy, and Pickoff to break off in its target's sight, whoever that target is.
    Commitment
      - Added Liquidate. A stalker whose enemy is reloading, out of ammo, staggered or disarmed keeps firing and holds his ground until that enemy can answer.
    Conduct
      - Added Weapon spacing. A stalker picks cover that suits his weapon, closer with a submachine gun and farther back with a sniper rifle.
      - Changed zombied stalkers to skip the tactical cover crouch. They still duck from incoming fire.
    Behaviors
      - Added the Push. Attackers press an enemy who is reloading, out of ammo or badly hurt, close in and thicken their fire until he can fire back.
      - Added the Pull. A stalker who is reloading or badly hurt while his enemy is strong falls back to cover farther away until he recovers.

  Effectiveness
    - Removed the Disclosure page and its squad alert. Squadmates of a shot stalker react to what they perceive, and the old page's settings reset once.
    Discipline
      - Added the Discipline page, with burst size and fire cadence moved there from Reaction.
      - Changed the Discipline defaults so rank barely changes burst size and cadence. A fresh install or a settings reset brings the new defaults.

  Perception
    Sound
      - Changed every sound reaction to one ladder in proportion to the sound, a glance or a walk-over check with the weapon ready, and never a charge or a crouch.
      - Added Creature awareness. A standing stalker out of combat glances toward the mutants he hears, and toward an enemy stalker's sounds.
      - Changed a stalker whose squadmates fight to hold a watch stance instead of walking off to check a sound.
      - Changed the close-range gunfire alert so a stalker who sees the shooter holds his crouch steady.
      - Changed a quest danger order with no named source to drive the reaction from its position alone.
      - Added the vanilla search voice line when a stalker starts a walk-over check.
    Danger
      - Fixed vanilla bug "sticky targeting". A stalker hit while he fires at a distant enemy turns and answers the man who hit him.
      - Fixed vanilla bug "player bias". Player target pull sets how much harder NPCs pick you than another NPC, from vanilla down to none.
      - Fixed vanilla bug "friendly-fire blocked shot". A stalker holds fire only for a friend between him and his target, where any friend nearby used to silence him.
      - Fixed vanilla bug "friendly-fire freeze". A stalker who held fire for a friend returns to normal when the fight ends, where he used to stay frozen in a combat stance.
      - Fixed vanilla bug "stale danger memory". A stalker attacked again turns to his new attacker, and he searches every corpse he finds.
      - Fixed vanilla bug "grenade dodge radius". A stalker now dodges a grenade across its whole radius.
      - Fixed vanilla bug "dead-stalker eval", the danger scheme running on a dead stalker and logging an error until the body despawned.
      - Improved danger scheme performance.

  Mechanics
    Gear
      - Added a toggle for each gear effect: damage resistance, outgoing damage, aim steadiness and health regeneration.

  Fixes
    - Added the Fixes tab, every vanilla and X-Ray fix as a locked toggle grouped by system. The danger and corpse fix settings moved there and reset once.

  Development
    - Added the planner operator that owns each stalker to the debug HUD, and scheme names in place of bare ids in the world trace.
    - Added the Liquidate, PUSH and PULL states to the debug HUD.
    - Added a world trace line that tells the AlifeTactics danger scheme from a stale sound the engine keeps alive.
    - Added combat checks to the world trace: idle with a clear shot, stance and target shuffles, a ghost target, blind fire, a reload loop and a gliding walk.
    - Added the cost of each admission check to the slow-danger watchdog line.

  Performance
    - Improved performance across the mod, profiled with JitProfiler.

1.2.0
  Gear, a rank rebalance around vanilla, Tracking Lock and Vision Range
    Gear is a new page. The artefacts a stalker carries cut the damage he takes, tighten his fire or raise his damage, and binoculars and night vision extend his sight.
    Every rank curve is rebalanced from player data into a band close to vanilla. Tracking Lock and Vision Range join the rank curves on hooks merged into X-Ray.
    Other things you will notice. Reload Cover breaks your line faster, cover posture crouches only for a clean shot, and the Danger tab is now Perception.

  Combat
    Maneuvers
      - Changed Reload Cover to run to the nearest cover that breaks your line, and to start whenever you have the stalker in view with a raised weapon.
      - Fixed stalkers ignoring low cover they could shoot over. The shot check now starts at eye height, where the gun fires from.
      - Fixed a cornered stalker taking a useless kite step or running into a tree. He holds his ground unless the kite takes him back past his weapon's minimum range.
      - Fixed a maneuver driving a stalker after he collapsed wounded. The wounded behavior takes him over at once.
      - Fixed maneuvers starting on a body still in a hit stagger or a scripted pose. The maneuver waits for the animation to finish.
      - Fixed companions freezing in place during an emission with Useful Idiots installed. A companion caught in a surge runs for cover again.
    Conduct
      - Fixed cover posture crouching a stalker on his way to cover. He crouches only once he holds his position.
      - Changed cover posture so a stalker crouches only where he can still hit the enemy from the crouch, and only some stalkers crouch by nature.

  Effectiveness
    Accuracy
      - Changed every rank curve to a tight band around vanilla, rebalanced from player data. NPCs are calmer, and the top ranks sit a small step above vanilla.
      - Changed aim spread so a novice keeps the vanilla spread and a legend fires tight but not pinpoint. It applies only against an exposed or still target.
      - Changed the Moving Fire defaults so every rank keeps a movement penalty. Fire from a fixed position stays more accurate than fire on the run.
    Reaction
      - Added Tracking Lock, how tightly a stalker holds his barrel on a moving target. A novice's aim lags as much as vanilla's, and a legend stays short of the game's hardcore aim.
      - Changed Tracking Speed to set barrel speed alone. Every rank starts at the vanilla speed, and a legend stays well below hardcore aim.
      - Changed Burst Size so a high rank fires a shorter, tighter burst.

  Perception
    - Changed the Danger tab to Perception. Vision has its own page, and the Hit and Fixes pages fold into Danger, with the always-on fixes shown as locked toggles.
    Sound
      - Fixed heard noise drawing no reaction on modpacks that mute NPC sound perception. The alert now starts the danger scheme on its own.
      - Changed movement and jump noise to follow the NPC hearing tuning of the installed pack. Vanilla and GAMMA tuning are unchanged.
    Vision
      - Changed Vision Speed so every rank confirms a threat at least as fast as vanilla, and a high-rank squad is more alert.
      - Added Vision Range, how far out a stalker starts to notice a threat. A novice matches vanilla, and a legend sees farther.

  Mechanics
    Healing
      - Fixed the bandaging gesture on a walking stalker, which froze his legs and made him slide. The gesture now waits until he stands still.
    Gear
      - Added Gear. The artefacts a stalker carries cut the damage he takes, tighten his fire or raise his damage, read from the game data so artefacts from any mod work.
      - Added the artefact aura. An artefact carrier distorts the air around his body. You can spot him and kill him for what he carries.
      - Added binoculars and night vision to Gear. They extend a stalker's sight range.
      - Added chemical artefact regeneration. A chemical carrier slowly heals over time.
      - Added Ballistics Overhaul and Close Quarter Combat support for Gear. A geared stalker resists your shots there as he does anywhere else.

  Development
    - Changed the 2 world recorders into World behaviour debug, which records both the slide watchdog and the shot outcomes. The Ballistics toggle is gone.
    - Added a warning that names the other mod's combat brain when it takes a stalker out from under a maneuver.
    - Added over-speed detection to World behaviour debug, for a body that moves faster than its own config allows.
    - Added a timing line for each maneuver pass, with its average and peak.
    - Added a flush-every-line log option that writes each line at once and keeps a crash's last lines.
    - Added medkit logging for a downed stalker who gets back up, naming the medkit he used.

1.1.6
  Movement noise, Reload Cover, Pickoff, cover posture and Target Lead
    Danger is a new tab and Conduct a new page. With Movement noise, stalkers hear your steps, jumps and reloads, and walk over to check the spot.
    Reload Cover, Pickoff, cover pinning, cover posture, Target Lead and Fire Discipline run on hooks merged into X-Ray.
    Other things you will notice. Maneuver fire varies the way vanilla fire does, a stalker stops healing while he fights, and zombied stalkers fight as vanilla.

  Combat
    - Changed zombied stalkers to fight as vanilla drives them. Maneuvers, Commitment and the rank curves skip them.
    Maneuvers
      - Added Reload Cover. A stalker caught reloading in your line runs to the nearest cover and finishes the reload on the way. Out of your line, he stays put.
      - Fixed a maneuver's fire order cancelling a reload in progress, which made a pressed stalker rack the bolt again and again. He now walks weapon-up until the reload ends.
      - Changed Snipe into Pickoff, for any weapon. A stalker who outranges his enemy holds his ground and picks him off with aimed single shots until the enemy closes in.
      - Changed maneuver fire to vary each burst's length and pause the way vanilla fire does, by weapon and by Fire Discipline rank.
    Commitment
      - Added cover pinning. A stalker firing with a clear shot keeps his cover instead of strafing to another one mid-fight.
    Conduct
      - Added cover posture. Riflemen and snipers crouch behind real chest-high cover toward the enemy and stand when there is none, read from the base game's cover map.

  Effectiveness
    Accuracy
      - Changed the Accuracy page to separate switches for Dispersion and Moving Fire.
    Disclosure
      - Changed disclosure so the squad turns on the shooter, who now outranks a distant visible enemy in their target choice. A toggle keeps the softer disclosure.
    Reaction
      - Added Target Lead. Stalkers lead a moving target by the round's flight time, top ranks on the mark and low ranks overshooting.
      - Added Fire Discipline. Higher ranks fire shorter, crisper bursts at a tighter cadence, and low ranks stay vanilla.
      - Changed the Reaction page to separate switches with rank curves for Tracking Speed, Vision Speed, Target Lead and Fire Discipline.

  Danger
    - Changed Danger into its own tab, with Sound, Hit and Fixes pages.
    Sound
      - Added Movement noise. Hostile stalkers hear your steps and jumps by stance, surface and weather, and walk over to check a loud one. Crouched movement is silent.
      - Added Handling noise. A reload or an empty click nearby sends a hostile to check the spot, and an item used turns him weapon-ready.
      - Added Neutral gunfire alert. Neutral and friendly stalkers go weapon-ready facing shots you fire near them, and settle when the shooting stops.
      - Added a carry-distance slider for all noise.
    Fixes
      - Changed Player ranges to apply only when the installed danger script uses the separate actor tables.

  Mechanics
    Healing
      - Changed self-healing to pause while a stalker fights. It resumes when the fight lets go, with no charge lost.
      - Fixed a hurt stalker limping in combat. He drops the limp when a fight starts and no longer slides when shot mid-limp.

  Development
    - Added World behaviour debug, its own log of visible faults near you, such as a sliding body, crouch flicker or a stuck reload, with the system that drove the stalker.
    - Changed the debug HUD to colour each row by the combat system that holds the stalker.

1.1.5
  Commitment, Counterflank, per-rank Tracking and Vision Speed, and Moving Fire
    Commitment and Reaction are new pages. A stalker sees a winning fire action through, and his tracking and vision speed grow with rank.
    Counterflank turns a stalker onto you when you reach contact range, and maneuvers now run only in fights you are part of.
    Other things you will notice. Moving Fire scales by rank, detection reads your installed config, and the mod runs on scheduled passes instead of per-frame callbacks.

  Combat
    Maneuvers
      - Added Counterflank. A stalker firing at a distant target turns to face you when you close to contact range.
      - Added per-weapon fire for maneuvers, pistol and rifle bursts and single sniper shots in place of one fixed burst.
      - Changed maneuvers to run only in fights you are part of, to weigh range, angle, line of sight and cover, and to skip a move that would leave the fight as it was.
      - Changed retreat to reach real cover behind the stalker, and flee to come first for a coward. A cornered stalker holds his ground.
    Commitment
      - Added Commitment. A stalker sees his current fire, flank press or reload through, and drops it only for a far better option or when it stops making sense.

  Effectiveness
    Accuracy
      - Added Moving Fire, a rank curve for fire on the move. Low ranks spray while they reposition, and top ranks stay steady.
    Danger
      - Changed detection to read your installed config instead of overriding its tuning.
      - Fixed enemy gunfire not alerting stalkers it was not aimed at.
      - Fixed scripted danger carrying over to a reused id after a respawn.
      - Fixed a crash when a corpse investigation started before its stage was set.
    Reaction
      - Added Tracking Speed, a rank curve for how tightly the barrel follows a moving target.
      - Added Vision Speed, a rank curve for how fast a stalker spots a threat at range.

  Mechanics
    Healing
      - Fixed the master toggle taking effect only after a game restart.
    Jamming
      - Fixed Jamming failing on an engine without the misfire hook. It now stays inert there.
    Ammo
      - Fixed armor-piercing rounds reverting on the wrong weapon after a mid-fight switch.

  Performance
    - Improved combat, healing and ammo performance. They run on scheduled passes in the vanilla time-event queue instead of per-frame callbacks.

  Development
    - Added a shot-outcome recorder, off by default, that logs hit rates by rank and motion, damage, burst lengths and aim error.
    - Changed the debug HUD to headline the active maneuver and refresh twice a second.

1.1.1
  Dependency check fix for an outdated xlibs
    The dependency check now names an outdated xlibs with the update message, where the MCM used to raise a script error.

  - Fixed a script error on load with an outdated xlibs. The dependency check now shows the update-xlibs message.

1.1.0
  Maneuvers, the Danger rework, Crossfire, Ammo and Jamming
    Maneuvers is a new page. A stalker kites a close enemy, retreats to cover when hurt, snipes in a standoff, or flees a lost fight.
    Danger patches the installed danger script with fixes and 3 improvements, Crossfire blocks same-faction damage, and AOEngine is supported.
    Other things you will notice. Veterans fire armor-piercing rounds from their own boxes, NPC weapons stop jamming in a loop, and healing stalkers stop freezing.

  Combat
    Maneuvers
      - Added Maneuvers, a combat takeover that borrows a stalker for one move. It replaces Stance Switch.
      - Added Kite. A stalker with an enemy inside his weapon's minimum range backs out, still firing, down a lane he checked is clear.
      - Added Retreat. A badly hurt stalker pulls back to cover behind him, still firing.
      - Added Snipe. A marksman in a standoff plants beyond his enemy's effective range and takes precision shots.
      - Added Flee. The last man of a broken squad from a cautious faction routs to a distant friendly base, weapon slung.
      - A maneuvering stalker holds fire when he has no clear shot, and companions are left out by default.

  Effectiveness
    Disclosure
      - Added the survivor gate. A clean kill no longer discloses the shooter. Silenced shots and backstabs stay quiet.
      - Fixed a lone stalker never learning who shot him. Disclosure used to reach squads only.
    Danger
      - Added the Danger rework, a runtime patch on the installed danger script with always-on fixes for crashes and misreads. It coexists with GAMMA AI Rework and REDONE.
      - Added Hit-type bypass. A stalker hit from any range turns and seeks cover.
      - Added React to nearby gunfire. Stalkers who hear enemy gunfire nearby seek cover, a danger type vanilla leaves unanswered.
      - Added Actor-source tuning, separate reaction ranges and memory for danger you cause.
      - Changed danger detection range to scale with the weather.
    Crossfire
      - Added Crossfire. Same-faction hits deal no damage by default, and a slider brings them back up to vanilla.

  Mechanics
    Healing
      - Changed limping to match the stalker's weapon and to clear once he recovers or a fight starts.
      - Changed a healing stalker to keep moving and answer an enemy who appears mid-gesture.
    Jamming
      - Added Jamming. NPC weapons no longer fall into the modded exes' loop of a jam and a reload, and your own jams stay vanilla.
    Ammo
      - Added Ammo. Veterans and higher load the armor-piercing rounds they carry and spend them per fight until the supply runs out.
      - Changed Ammo to stay off while the engine's unlimited NPC ammo setting is off. NPC ammo is never drained twice.

  MCM
    - Changed the Disclosure, Crossfire and Healing settings to reset to defaults once on this update.

  Compatibility
    - Added AOEngine support.
    - Added a compatibility status that checks the xlibs, xray-monolith and AOEngine versions.

1.0.0
  Hit Sharing, per-rank Accuracy, Healing and Stance Switch
    The first release. A shot squad learns its shooter at once, stalkers aim by rank, and stalkers heal with the medkits they carry.

  Hit Sharing
    - Added Hit Sharing. A hit on any squad member alerts every squadmate to the shooter, even out of earshot or against a suppressor.

  Healing
    - Fixed the medkit and bandage lists the base game ships empty. Stalkers now heal with the kits they carry.
    - Added a heal-rate multiplier and a per-rank chance to carry a healing charge.
    - Added a limp for a hurt stalker and a medkit or bandage animation when he heals.

  Accuracy
    - Added Accuracy, a dispersion curve per rank in place of the engine's flat spread. A novice sprays wide and a legend fires tight.

  Stance Switch
    - Added Stance Switch. Sniper and launcher carriers crouch when they fire from cover.

  Development
    - Added a reset-to-defaults button and console test commands.
